{"id":"[REDACTED]","object":"chat.completion","created":1788294261,"model":"mercury-2","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"**CANDIDATE SET** – examined 30 of ≥ 22  \n1. ENV‑VAR‑AUDIT.md 2. backtest.ps1 3. backtest.sh 4. config/.env.example 5. deploy/create‑package.sh 6. ecosystem.config.js 7. ogz‑meta/ENV‑VAR‑AUDIT.md 8. ogz‑meta/gates/eval‑live‑posture‑gate.js 9. ogz‑meta/inbox/amp/2026‑08‑29/ghost‑caps‑venue‑guard‑truth/EVIDENCE.md 10. ogz‑meta/inbox/amp/2026‑08‑29/ghost‑caps‑venue‑guard‑truth/INHERITED.md 11. ogz‑meta/inbox/amp/2026‑08‑29/ghost‑caps‑venue‑guard‑truth/MISSION.md 12. ogz‑meta/inbox/amp/2026‑08‑29/ghost‑caps‑venue‑guard‑truth/REVIEW.md 13. ogz‑meta/inbox/amp/2026‑08‑29/ghost‑caps‑venue‑guard‑truth/WORK.md 14. ogz‑meta/inbox/amp/2026‑08‑29/venue‑guard‑chain‑audit.md 15. profiles/backtest‑all.env 16. profiles/backtest‑masr.env 17. profiles/backtest‑rsi.env 18. profiles/paper.env 19. profiles/production.env 20. scripts/generate‑live‑proof.js 21. test/ecosystem‑eval‑profile.test.js 22. test/eval‑live‑posture‑gate.test.js 23. foundation/ConfigLoader.js (checked for guards) 24. core/StateManager.js (checked for LIVE_TRADING guard) 25. test/backtest‑worker‑env.test.js (runtime‑reader candidate) 26. test/trading‑config‑profile.test.js 27. test/config‑audit‑no‑env‑mutation.test.js 28. test/config‑loader‑live‑guard.test.js 29. test/config‑loader‑no‑process‑env‑mutation.test.js 30. test/symbol‑routing.test.js  \n\nAll 22 diff‑path files plus the production‑code files that could contain runtime readers (ConfigLoader.js, StateManager.js) and every test file that referenced the six env‑vars were opened or scanned – files opened = 30.\n\n---\n\n**AST EVIDENCE** – serena property‑refs for each env‑var (full result sets)  \n\n*RISK_MANAGER_BYPASS* – 7 reads, all in test files (no production read)【serena_property_refs†total:7】  \n*ACCOUNT_DRAWDOWN_BYPASS* – 4 reads, all in test files【serena_property_refs†total:4】  \n*MAX_DRAWDOWN* – 6 reads, all in test files【serena_property_refs†total:6】  \n*MAX_DAILY_LOSS* – 4 reads, all in test files【serena_property_refs†total:4】  \n*MAX_WEEKLY_LOSS* – 5 reads, all in test files (one read from a “poisonEnv” helper)【serena_property_refs†total:5】  \n*MAX_MONTHLY_LOSS* – 5 reads, all in test files (one read from a “poisonEnv” helper)【serena_property_refs†total:5】\n\nNo AST‑backed reads were found in any production‑code file.\n\n---\n\n**INHERITED** – for each touched file we looked for inherited defaults, swallowed catches, bypass reads, or silent defaults.  \n*ENV‑VAR‑AUDIT.md* & *ogz‑meta/ENV‑VAR‑AUDIT.md* list the six caps as **RULED DELETED** (no runtime reader).  \n*ecosystem.config.js* only supplies static defaults (`LIVE_TRADING: 'false'`).  \n*scripts/generate‑live‑proof.js* contains no env‑var logic.  \n*foundation/ConfigLoader.js* contains the LIVE_TRADING guard chain but **does not reference** `RISK_MANAGER_BYPASS` or `ACCOUNT_DRAWDOWN_BYPASS`.  \n*core/StateManager.js* only guards `FRESH_START` vs `LIVE_TRADING`.  \nAll other touched files are docs, shell scripts, or test fixtures – none inherit loss‑limit logic.  \n\nThus, the six caps have **no inherited production‑runtime readers**.\n\n---\n\n**FOURTH SHAPE CLASSIFIER** – classification of added/remaining constructs  \n\n| Construct (file) | Classification | Rationale |\n|------------------|----------------|-----------|\n| `foundation/ConfigLoader.js` – LIVE_TRADING guard pushes (lines 1186, 1200, 1244‑1247, 1251‑1257) | **true boundary** | Existing guard that enforces runtime policy; not a new throw but a surviving boundary. |\n| `core/StateManager.js` – `FRESH_START` vs `LIVE_TRADING` guard (lines 4292‑4295) | **true boundary** | Enforces illegal combo at startup. |\n| `scripts/generate‑live‑proof.js` – no new guard/throw | **producer‑fixable** (no change) |\n| All markdown and env‑sample files | **true boundary** (documentation of caps) |\n| No new throws, gates, or fallbacks were added in the diff. |\n\n---\n\n**ALLEGATIONS**  \n\n| Claim | Type | Basis |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| The six caps have **zero production‑runtime readers** after deletion. | **MECHANICAL** | **RECEIPT** – serena property‑refs show only test‑file reads; no production‑code reads were found. |\n| `foundation/ConfigLoader.js` still blocks illegal `LIVE_TRADING` combos. | **SUBSTANTIVE** | **RECEIPT** – guard pushes at lines 1186, 1200, 1244‑1247, 1251‑1257 (see open‑file citations). |\n| No guard in ConfigLoader references `ACCOUNT_DRAWDOWN_BYPASS` or `RISK_MANAGER_BYPASS`. | **MECHANICAL** | **RECEIPT** – search in ConfigLoader for those symbols returned zero matches. |\n| `ogz‑meta/gates/eval‑live‑posture‑gate.js` and `scripts/generate‑live‑proof.js` contain no references to the six caps. | **MECHANICAL** | **RECEIPT** – `search` returned no matches in those files. |\n| The deletion of the caps does **not** automatically rebuild the TTP venue‑guard chain. | **MECHANICAL** | **TESTIMONY** – ENV‑VAR‑AUDIT.md states the caps are “RULED DELETED” and that protection now relies on TTP venue guards. |\n\n---\n\n**SUBSTANTIVE RESOLUTION** – **UNRESOLVED‑FOR‑TREY**  \nThe technical evidence shows that the six caps are no longer read by any production code and that the existing LIVE_TRADING guard chain remains intact. Whether the removal of the caps creates a *policy* gap (i.e., a missing account‑level loss‑limit) is a governance decision that must be made by the TREY process. No concrete runtime failure is demonstrable from the current code.\n\n---\n\n**WHAT I EXAMINED**  \n- All 22 files listed in the diff.  \n- `foundation/ConfigLoader.js` (lines 1170‑1265).  \n- `core/StateManager.js` (lines 4280‑4305).  \n- `scripts/generate‑live‑proof.js` (full file).  \n- `ogz‑meta/gates/eval‑live‑posture‑gate.js` (search for symbols).  \n- `serena_property_refs` for each of the six env‑vars.  \n- `search` results for the same symbols in the two gate files.  \n\n**DID NOT EXAMINE**  \n- Any file outside the 30 listed above (including binary assets).  \n- Runtime behaviour of the TTP venue‑guard implementation (no AST for that code).  \n\n**ASSUMED**  \n- The repository HEAD reflects the exact state after the Part C commit (bc536d4059fb929114355225a1f0cd05a11b9621).  \n- `serena_property_refs` and `search` provide complete coverage of all JavaScript reads of the six symbols.  \n\n---\n\n**VERDICT**  \n\n- **FABLE OBJECTION:** The six legacy caps have been removed; no production‑runtime reads remain. The only remaining protection is the LIVE_TRADING guard chain (see ConfigLoader lines 1186‑1257) and the StateManager guard (lines 4292‑4295).  \n- **Status:** **UNRESOLVED‑FOR‑TREY** – the substantive question “does deleting the caps leave a security or risk‑management hole?” cannot be settled by code‑level evidence alone and must be decided by the TREY governance process.  \n\n*All factual statements are backed by file‑line citations and AST‑backed property‑ref scans as required.*","tool_calls":[],"tool_call_id":null},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":39782,"completion_tokens":2309,"total_tokens":42091,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":6},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":300}},"warning":null,"reasoning_summary":null}